B1  the Bullet   (PRE-REGISTERED: the gate most likely to kill)
====================================================================================================
DB1's transcribed criteria: (i) Sigma_c >= 3 x ICM column swept in one passage;
                            (ii) G Sigma_c^2 >= rho_ICM v^2 at v = 4700 km/s
RB1 gate 4: the lensing peak sits with the galaxies (model 14 / 10 kpc); the gas sits hundreds of kpc away.

cluster   M_gas        M_star      M_cold = 5.41 (gas+star)   Sigma_c (Plummer b=200 kpc)
main      2.000e+14  1.196e+13  1.1467e+15                 9.1252e+09 Msun/kpc^2
sub       2.320e+13  4.000e+12  1.4715e+14                 1.1710e+09 Msun/kpc^2
ICM central density (main gas 2.0e14 in a Plummer b = 200 kpc, PROVISIONAL): 5.9683e+06 Msun/kpc^3
ICM column over a 1 Mpc path (PROVISIONAL):                                  1.5915e+09 Msun/kpc^2
  (i)  needs Sigma_c >= 4.7746e+09 ; the solid's column 9.1252e+09  -> PASSES
  (ii) needs Sigma_c >= 5.5366e+09 ; the solid's column 9.1252e+09  -> PASSES
  NOTE: DB1's two tests are self-gravity tests. They are blind to solidity -- a solid
        passes them and still cannot interpenetrate. That is the point of this gate.

B1a  structural. A solid's map is a homeomorphism: material elements keep their neighbours.
     The two clusters have passed through each other, so their media must have interpenetrated.
     The subcluster's cold mass is 1.472e+14 Msun (5.41 x its gas + stars); RB1 places it with the
     subcluster's galaxies, which are now INSIDE the main cluster's radius. The interpenetrated
     cold mass required by the data is therefore 1.472e+14 Msun at least. A homeomorphism
     cannot deliver any nonzero value.
     Equivalently: at the observed epoch the two media occupy the same volume, so the map from
     the reference configuration to the present one is 2-to-1 there. A solid has no such map.

